   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the town/village of East Rochester, county\nof Monroe to hire Karol Hughes to fill a full-time competitive position with\nthe town/village of East Rochester police department",
    "basePrintNo": "S7376",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7376-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Monroe County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7376\n\nSPONSOR: BROUK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the town/village of East Rochester,\ncounty of Monroe to hire Karol Hughes to fill a full-time competitive\nposition with the town/village of East Rochester police department\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill authorizes the appointment of Karol Hughes, of the Village of\nEast Rochester, to a full-time competitive position as a police officer\nof the village.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 Notwithstanding section 58 of the Civil Service Law, the\nVillage of East Rochester is authorized to appoint Karol Hughes to a\nfull-time competitive position as a police officer of the village.\n\nSection 2 states Karol Hughes shall still be subject to the merit and\nfitness provisions of the civil service law applicable to full-time\npolice officers.\n\nSection 3 sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will allow Karol Hughes, currently a part-time police officer\nfor the Village of East Rochester, to be appointed in the competitive\nclass of civil service as a full-time police officer in the village,\nnotwithstanding the 35-year-old limitation set forth in section 58 of\nthe Civil Service Law.\n\n \nPRIOR HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
