    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Monroe County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7376A\n\nSPONSOR: BROUK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing Karol Hughes to take the competitive\ncivil service examination for the position of police officer and be\nplaced on the eligible list for employment as a full-time police officer\nfor the town/village of East Rochester\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill authorizes Karol Hughes, a part-time police officer, with the\ntown/village of East Rochester police department to take the civil exam-\nination.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 Notwithstanding section 58 of the Civil Service Law, the\nVillage of East Rochester is authorized to appoint Karol Hughes to a\nfull-time competitive position as a police officer of the village.\n\nSection 2 states Karol Hughes shall still be subject to the merit and\nfitness provisions of the civil service law applicable to full-time\npolice officers.\n\nSection 3 sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will allow Karol Hughes, currently a part-time police officer\nfor the Village of East Rochester, to be appointed in the competitive\nclass of civil service as a full-time police officer in the village,\nnotwithstanding the 35-year-old limitation set forth in section 58 of\nthe Civil Service Law.\n\n \nPRIOR HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
